{"name":"Bateau","hex":"#1b7598","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bateau","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, flat-bottomed type of boat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bateau"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bateau","blocks":[{"text":"A bateau or batteau is a shallow-draft, flat-bottomed boat which was used extensively across North America, especially in the colonial period and in the fur trade. It was traditionally pointed at both ends but came in a wide variety of sizes. The name derives from the French word, bateau, which is simply the word for boat and the plural, bateaux, follows the French, an unusual construction for an English plural. In the southern United States, the term is still used to refer to flat-bottomed boats, including those elsewhere called johnboats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/BateauReplicas2013.JPG/330px-BateauReplicas2013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bateau","wikidata":"Q4868744"},{"title":"Bateau (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"Bateau was a steakhouse in Seattle, in the U.S. state of Washington. The restaurant was founded by chef Renee Erickson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/89/Bateau_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bateau_(restaurant)","wikidata":"Q111169423"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Colonial_Bateau_Replicas.JPG/500px-Colonial_Bateau_Replicas.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Colonial_Bateau_Replicas.JPG/1280px-Colonial_Bateau_Replicas.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Colonial_Bateau_Replica